  "title": "Albanese and Labour Party at Odds Over Euthanasia Telehealth Policy",
  "summary": "Anthony Albanese, the prime minister of Australia, addressed a Labour Party conference in Adelaide, emphasizing the need for a united government and a commitment to policy change. The debate surrounding euthanasia and telehealth consultations was part of a broader effort to reform Labor’s national platform.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Labour Party announced plans to overturn a Howard-era law banning telehealth consultations for euthanasia.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Albanese highlighted the need for a unified government and policy change in response to recent political challenges.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government is set to introduce legislation based on changes to the ALP platform.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
